{"id":"qzpyq-chemistry-biomolecules-biomolecules-test-1","_quizrrTestId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa","title":"Biomolecules - Test 1","questions":[{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a09de","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a09de","q":"Match List I with List II\n\\(<table class=\"qx-match-list qx-match-table\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td></td><td>List - I</td><td></td><td>List - II</td></tr><tr><td>A.</td><td>\\alpha - Glucose and \\alpha - Galactose</td><td>I.</td><td>Functional isomers</td></tr><tr><td>B.</td><td>\\alpha - Glucose and \\beta - Glucose</td><td>II.</td><td>Homologous</td></tr><tr><td>C.</td><td>\\alpha - Glucose and \\alpha - Fructose</td><td>III.</td><td>Anomers</td></tr><tr><td>D.</td><td>\\alpha - Glucose and \\alpha - Ribose</td><td>IV.</td><td>Epimers</td></tr></table>\\)\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:","options":["A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II","A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II","A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a09e3","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a09e3","q":"Glycosidic linkage between ${C}_{1}$ of $\\alpha$-glucose and ${C}_{2}$ of $\\beta$-fructose is found in","options":["Maltose","<p>Sucrose</p><p></p>","Lactose","amylose"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<blockquote><p>Sucrose</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-8ea23a06db8aa15c.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 274px; height: 130px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8ea23a06db8aa15c.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8ea23a06db8aa15c.png\"></p><p>Sucrose is composed of a molecule of glucose joined to a molecule of fructose by an $\\alpha - 1, \\beta - 2$-gIycosidic linkage.</p><p>~</p><p>Mannose is a sugar monomer of the aldohexose series of carbohydrates. It is a $C - 2$ epimer of glucose.</p><p>Fructose, or fruit sugar, is a ketonic simple sugar found in many plants, where it is often bonded to glucose to form the disaccharide sucrose.</p><p>Lactose is composed of a molecule of galactose joined to a molecule of glucose by a $\\beta - 1, 4$-gIycosidic linkage. It is a reducing sugar that is found in milk.</p><p></p></blockquote>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a09e8","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a09e8","q":"<p>The correct sequence of amino acids present in the tripeptide given below is:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-88ac9371d2649718.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 393px; height: 190px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-88ac9371d2649718.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-88ac9371d2649718.png\"></p>","options":["Val - Ser - Thr","Leu - Ser - Thr","Thr - Ser - Val","Thr - Ser - Leu"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Amino acids are organic compounds that contain amino and carboxyl functional groups, along with a side chain specific to each amino acid. The key elements of an amino acid are carbon, hydrogen, oxygen, and nitrogen, although other elements are found in the side chains of certain amino acids.</p><p>Peptides are short chains of amino acids linked by peptide bonds</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-237fa73f