\right)}_{2}O}^{yeq . of}$ acetyl derivative</p><p>(iii) Glucose $\\mathop{\\to}_{{\\left({CH}_{3}CO\\right)}_{2}O}^{zeq . of}$ acetyl derivative &#39;$x$&#39; , &#39;$y$&#39; and &#39;$z$&#39; in these reactions are respectively.</p>","options":["$5, 4$ &amp; $6$","$4, 6$ &amp; $5$","$4, 5$ &amp; $5$","$5, 6$ &amp; $5$"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa","_marksId":"648b5a67417cc3fb48d66981","question":"<p>Consider the following reactions :</p><p>(i) Glucose $+ ROH\\overset{dryHCI}{\\to}Acetal\\mathop{\\to}_{{\\left({CH}_{3}CO\\right)}_{2}}^{xeq . of}$ acetyl derivative</p><p>(ii) Glucose $\\overset{Ni / {H}_{2}}{\\to}A\\mathop{\\to}_{{\\left({CH}_{3}CO\\right)}_{2}O}^{yeq . of}$ acetyl derivative</p><p>(iii) Glucose $\\mathop{\\to}_{{\\left({CH}_{3}CO\\right)}_{2}O}^{zeq . of}$ acetyl derivative &#39;$x$&#39; , &#39;$y$&#39; and &#39;$z$&#39; in these reactions are respectively.</p>"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a01","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a01","q":"Glucose and Galactose are having identical configuration in all the positions except position.","options":["$C - 3$","$C - 4$","$C - 5$","$C - 2$"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"The structures of Glucose and Galactose are:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-ee7903de83e63689.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 250px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-ee7903de83e63689.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-ee7903de83e63689.png\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-8e47b0cf2882fbe1.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 239px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8e47b0cf2882fbe1.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-8e47b0cf2882fbe1.png\"><br />Hence, Glucose and Galactose differ only in the arrangement at $C - 4$ carbon","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a06","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a06","q":"Identify correct conversion during acidic hydrolysis from the following :\n(A) starch gives galactose.\n(B) cane sugar gives equal amount of glucose and fructose.\n(C) milk sugar gives glucose and galactose.\n(D) amylopectin gives glucose and fructose.\n(E) amylose gives only glucose. Choose the correct answer from the options given below :","options":["(A), (B) and (C) only","(B), (C) and (E) only","(C), (D) and (E) only","(B), (C) and (D) only"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"$(\\mathrm{A})$ Starch $\\xrightarrow{\\mathrmH^{+} / \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}}$ Glucose\n(B) Cane sugar $\\xrightarrow{\\mathrmH^{+} / \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}}$ glucose + fructose (Sucrose) $50 \\% \\quad 50 \\%$\n(C) Milk sugar $\\xrightarrow{\\mathrmH^{+} / \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}}$ glucose + galactose (Lactose)\n(D) Amylopectin $\\xrightarrow{\\mathrmH^{+} / \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}}$ Glucose\n(E) Amylose $\\xrightarrow{\\mathrmH^{+} / \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}}$ Glucose\nSo, correct options are B,C,and E only.","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a0b","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a0b","q":"Which one of the following is correct structure for cytosine ?","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fques