es denaturation of its protein resulting in loss of its quaternary, tertiary and secondary structures.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">But the primary structure (representing the sequence of $\\alpha$ amino acids) remains intact.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hence option A is the answer.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a15","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a15","q":"Which one of the following is a water soluble vitamin, that is not excreted easily?","options":["& $Vitamin{B}_{2}$","$Vitamin{B}_{1}$","$Vitamin{B}_{6}$","$Vitamin{B}_{12}$"],"answer":3,"answers":[3],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"B group vitamins and vitamin C are soluble in water except vitamin $\\mathrm{B}_{12}$ all are excreted easily.","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a1a","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a1a","q":"Which of the following statements is correct?","options":["Gluconic acid can form cyclic (acetal/hemiacetal) structure","Gluconic acid is a dicarboxylic acid","Gluconic acid is a partial oxidation product of glucose","Gluconic acid is obtained by oxidation of glucose with $HN{O}_{3}$"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a1f","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a1f","q":"<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-693bc78d4817d2e3.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 203px; height: 215px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-693bc78d4817d2e3.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-693