></p><p>Represents~$\\alpha ‐ D ‐ ( - )$~Fructofuranose</p><p>Structure</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_main%252Fe809c7e7-0669-466c-b690-029f2faa02ee-9894443_8.PNG%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=qxfig138\" style=\"width: 264px; height: 197px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e0b0c58e14fd8d01.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e0b0c58e14fd8d01.png\"></p><p>Represents $\\beta ‐ D ‐ ( - )$ Fructofuranose</p><p>So, the correct option is D</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a29","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a29","q":"A polysaccharide &#39;$X$&#39;~on boiling with dil ${H}_{2}{SO}_{4}$ at $393K$ under $2 - 3atm$ pressure yields &#39;$Y$&#39; &#39;$Y$&#39; on treatment with bromine water gives gluconic acid. &#39;$X$&#39; contains $\\beta$-glycosidic linkages only. Compound &#39;$X$&#39;& is :","options":["starch","cellulose","amylose","amylopectin"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Cellulose,& \\left({C}_{6}{H}_{10}{O}_{5}\\right)n$</p><p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_main%252F328484c3-7a57-49cd-810b-e7f5ee274014-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia \\text{ and } clean=1 \\text{ and } v=qxfig138\" style=\"width: 322px; height: 200px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-5a613c162f375c58.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-5a613c162f375c58.png\"></p><p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_main%252Fb97a0eef-003a-4871-af8c-2d8eb85e6c0c-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia \\text{ and } clean=1 \\text{ and } v=qxfig138\" style=\"width: 189px; height: 250px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-586f0d7c6ef70ee7.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-586f0d7c6ef70ee7.png\"></p>$","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a2e","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a2e","q":"Type of amino acids obtained by hydrolysis of proteins is :","options":["$\\beta$","$\\alpha$","$\\delta$","$\\gamma$"],"answer":1,"answers":[1],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Proteins are natural polymers composed of $\\alpha$-amino acids which are connected by peptide linkages.</p><p>The smallest unit to which the protein can be broken down is called amino acids. The $\\alpha$-amino acids are the amino acids whose one carbon contains both the amino group $\\left({NH}_{2}\\right)$ and the carboxyl group $\\left(COOH\\right)$. This type of carbon is called $\\alpha$-carbon. Thus, the amino acid that contains an $\\alpha$-carbon is called an $\\alpha$-amino acid.</p><p>Proteins upon acidic hydrolysis produce $\\alpha$-amino acids.</p><p>Hence, the answer is option B.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa","_resolvedFrom":"official_bank_unique","_marksId":"6682bd2dba0e94a3c4025b02","question":"Type of amino acids obtained by hydrolysis of proteins is :","explanation":"<p>Proteins are natural polymers composed of $\\alpha$-amino acids which are connected by peptide linkages.</p><p>The smallest unit to which the protein can be broken down is called amino acids. The $\\alpha$-amino acids are the amino acids whose one carbon contains both the amino group $\\left({NH}_{2}\\right)$ and the carboxyl group $\\left(COOH\\right)$. This type of carbon is called $\\alpha$-carbon. Thus, the amino acid that contains an $\\alpha$-carbon is called an $\\alpha$-amino acid.</p><p>Proteins upon acidic hydrolysis produce $\\alpha$-amino acids.</p><p>Hence, the answer is option B.</p>"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a33","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a33","q":"<p>Match List I and List II</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody> <tr> <td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\"> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">List I</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Vitamin</p> </td> <td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\"> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">List II</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Deficiency disease</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$A$</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Vitamin A</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$I$</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Beri-Beri</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$B$</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Thiamine</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$II$</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Cheilosis</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$C$</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Ascorbic acid</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$III$</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Xerophthalmia</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$D$</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Riboflavin</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">$IV$</td> <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Scurvy</td> </tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>","options":["<p>$A - III, B - I, C - IV, D - II$</p>","$A - IV, B - I, C - III, D - II$","$A - IV, B - II, C - III, D - I$","$A - III, B - II, C - IV, D - I$"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<blockquote><p>Vitamin A Deficiency: Xerophthalmia: With this condition, the eyes may become very dry and crusted, which may damage the cornea and retina.</p><p>Thiamine Deficiency: Beriberi is a disease in which the body does not have enough thiamine (vitamin B1).</p><p>Scurvy is a disease caused by a serious vitamin C(Ascorbic acid) deficiency</p><p>Riboflavin deficiency is often associated with cheilosis (chapping and fissuring of the lips). Riboflavin Deficiency. Riboflavin deficiency can be associated with various developmental abnormalities, including cleft lip.</p></blockquote>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a38","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a38","q":"Identify the number of structure/s from the following which can be correlated to D-glyceraldehyde. <img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-e89d26f0c0064bac.png?alt=media&v=stem2\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e89d26f0c0064bac.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-e89d26f0c0064bac.png\"><br/>","options":["four","one","two","three"],"answer":3,"answers":[3],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-03950f7b7f2b0e0d.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-03950f7b7f2b0e0d.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-03950f7b7f2b0e0d.png\"><br> In $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{D}^*-\\mathrm{OH}$ group in right hand side then D-configuration is assign","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a3d","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a3d","q":"The correct match between item $I$ and item $II$ is<br />~<table border=\"1\">\t<tbody> <tr> <td colspan=\"2\">Item $I$ (Compound)</td> <td colspan=\"2\">Item $II$ (Reagent)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>$a .$</td> <td>Lysine</td> <td>$p .$</td> <td>$1 -$naphthol</td> </tr> <tr> <td>$b .$</td> <td>Furfural</td> <td>$q .$</td> <td>Ninhydrin</td> </tr> <tr> <td>$c .$</td> <td>Benzyl alcohol</td> <td>$r .$</td> <td>${KMnO}_{4}$</td> </tr> <tr> <td>$d .$</td> <td>Styrene</td> <td>$s .$</td> <td>Ceric ammonium nitrate</td> </tr>\t</tbody></table>","options":["$a \\to q, b \\to r, c \\to s, d \\to p$","$a \\to q, b \\to p, c \\to s, d \\to r$","$a \\to r, b \\to p, c \\to q, d \\to s$","$a \\to q, b \\to p, c \\to r, d \\to s$"],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Lysine → Ninhydrin (this is given out by all the amino acids and Lysine is an amino acid.)<br /><br />Furfural$\\to1 -$naphthol.</p><p>Rapid furfural test is used to distinguish between glucose and fructose. In this test, the sugar solution is added to $1 -$naphthol and concentrated~$HCl$.<br /><br />Benzyl alcohol &rarr; ceric ammonium nitrate.<br /><br />Ceric ammonium nitrate test is used for testing of alcohols.<br /><br /><img height=\"83\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-55055c4c3672ec9b.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" width=\"128\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-55055c4c3672ec9b.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-55055c4c3672ec9b.png\"></p><p>Styrene undergoes oxidation when treated with ${KMnO}_{4}$.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a6c","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a6c","q":"In an oligopeptide named Alanylglycylphenyl alanyl isoleucine, the number of ${sp}^{2}$ hybridised carbons is& _____.","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>An oligopeptide is a short-chain peptide. The given& oligopeptide is a tripeptide.</p><p>The given Oligopeptide has the following structure</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-f04f0e131247c3f9.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 530px; height: 120px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-f04f0e131247c3f9.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-f04f0e131247c3f9.png\"></p><p>In& ${sp}^{2}$~hybridisation carbon can have one pi bond. The carbons marked with * are~${sp}^{2}$~carbons</p><p>It has $10{sp}^{2}$~hybridised $C$ atoms.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a71","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a71","q":"The number of oxygen present in a nucleotide formed from a base, that is present only in RNA is","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-book-c7c31058b8d373a7.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 248px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-c7c31058b8d373a7.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-book-c7c31058b8d373a7.png\"></p><p>Nucleotide with uracil& base present in RNA.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a76","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a76","q":"From the vitamins $A, {B}_{1}, {B}_{6}, {B}_{12}, C, D, E$ and $K$, the number vitamins that can be stored in our body is ______.","options":["","","",""],"answer":0,"answers":[0],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p>Fat-soluble vitamins are stored in the body's liver, fatty tissue, and muscles. The fat-soluble vitamins are vitamins $A, D, E, K$. These vitamins are absorbed more easily by the body in the presence of dietary fat. Water-soluble vitamins are not stored in the body. The only $B$ vitamin which is folound in liver is ${B}_{12}$.</p><p>Vitamins $A, D, E, K$ and ${B}_{12}$ are stored in liver and adipose tissue.</p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa"},{"id":"qz_69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a7b","_quizrrId":"69de4f922ee0e063d92a0a7b","q":"The number of chiral carbons present in sucrose is &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;.","options":["","","",""],"answer":"9","answers":["9"],"questionType":"numerical","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"JEE Main","source":"Quantrex PYQ Chapterwise","solution":"<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_main%252F67e4e1e5-293b-4fef-bbd2-8f8810423e9f-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=qxfig138\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 108px;\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F67e4e1e5-293b-4fef-bbd2-8f8810423e9f-image.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F67e4e1e5-293b-4fef-bbd2-8f8810423e9f-image.png?alt=media\"></p>","_bank":"quizrr_pyq_chapter","_testId":"69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5baa","correctValue":"9","_resolvedFrom":"official_bank_unique","_marksId":"648b5a68417cc3fb48d66b9d","question":"The number of chiral carbons present in sucrose is &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;.","explanation":"<p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fjee_main%252F67e4e1e5-293b-4fef-bbd2-8f8